# Citation metadata (D-18). CI validates this file with `cffconvert
# --validate` and cross-checks it against the README BibTeX block with
# scripts/check_citation.py, so edits here must be mirrored there.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: star_reacher
version: 0.8.0
# date-released is the UTC date the v0.8.0 tag was pushed, which is the date
# the release artifacts carry. It is a real release date, not the phase-close
# stamp it held while the version was prepared but unreleased: the release
# handoff's definition of done was met first (docs/release_handoff.md), with
# checklist item 3 discharged and item 11 closing on this tag.
# scripts/check_citation.py consumes only the year, so the README BibTeX block
# tracks this field through `year` alone.
date-released: 2026-07-27
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/JusHoya/star_reacher"
abstract: >-
  A small, deterministic six-degree-of-freedom space-mission simulator for
  launch vehicles, satellites, and lunar/Mars missions, built as a C++17/Eigen
  core behind a Python frontend, with every physical model derived, cited, and
  validated.
authors:
  - family-names: Hoyer
    given-names: Melvin
    name-suffix: III
